from functools import lru_cache


@lru_cache(maxsize=None)
def get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:
    if n == 0:
        return 0
    split_sum = (get_max_sum(n // 2) + get_max_sum(n // 3)
                 + get_max_sum(n // 4) + get_max_sum(n // 5))
    return max(split_sum, n)


assert get_max_sum(60) == 106
```

I kept the n/5 term. The team note says to drop it, but without that term f(60) comes out to 68, not 106, so the required assert would fail. With the n/5 term, the recurrence gives f(60) = max(44 + 28 + 18 + 16, 60) = 106.

